<title>POLAND: NBP DRAINS PLN 689 MLN FROM POLISH MONEY MARKET.</title>
<headline>NBP DRAINS PLN 689 MLN FROM POLISH MONEY MARKET.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Poland drained 689 million zlotys from the market through a reverse NBP-bill repurchase auction after banks bid to place 697 million with the central bank, the NBP said.</p>
<p>The bank drained the market for one day at a maximum rate of 21.50 percent, up from 21.30 percent on December 11.</p>
<p>The average accepted rate was 21.29 percent.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 2 653 9700</p>
</text>
